# SVG icons

Do **not** store reusable icons as static `.svg` assets imported via `<img>`.

ui-kit icons (`UiIcon` / `left-icon-name` on `UiButton`) are fine. Custom SVGs are Vue SFC components.

## Required pattern

- App icons: `apps/<app>/src/components/icons/` (domain subfolders like `aml/`, `projects/` when needed).
- Shared icons: `shared/components/` (e.g. blockchain).
- Each icon is a Vue SFC wrapping inline SVG.
- Prefer `fill="currentColor"` / `stroke="currentColor"` so color is set via CSS `color` at the call site.
- Set size via `width` / `height` on the SVG (or CSS), not hardcoded hex fills — unless the icon is inherently multi-color.

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" fill="none">
	<path d="..." fill="currentColor" />
</svg>

<!-- ❌ BAD: hardcoded color, not reusable -->
<path fill="rgb(48,51,69)" />

<!-- ❌ BAD: img asset -->
<img :src="iconUrl" />
```

Usage:

```vue
<icon-arrow-back class="back-icon" />
```

```scss
.back-icon {
	color: $grey;
}
```
